      "widgets_values": [
        1280,
        720,
        "Relight this exact photograph as a total blackout. Every light source is switched OFF: ceiling lights, lamps, pendants, practical fixtures, neon and signage, TVs, monitors and phone screens, candles, car headlights and street lights. Windows and glass show no daylight, no glow and no reflections of lit surroundings; there is no ambient fill or sky light. The scene falls into near-total darkness with deep, crushed blacks. The ONLY light is a single off-camera flashlight beam coming in from one side of the frame, a narrow cool-white cone that lights a small patch of the scene with a hard hot-spot and soft falloff, with subtle volumetric dust and haze visible inside the beam. Everything outside the beam is almost black, with only faint shapes. Keep the exact same composition, camera framing, lens and perspective, room geometry, furniture, people, faces, poses, clothing and props, pixel-aligned with the original. Do not add, remove or move any object or person; do not show the flashlight or who holds it. Photorealistic low-light photo with natural sensor noise, no text, no watermark.",
