        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "BLACKOUT DATASET BUILDER  (run with Ctrl+Enter)\n\nEVERY CLIP GOES THROUGH TWO STEPS:\n\nSTEP 1 - STILLS (on Magnific, outside Comfy)\n  An agent makes 10 Blackout stills of the clip's first frame\n  on Magnific (Nano Banana Pro, 750 Magnific credits per clip) and\n  drops them in input/blackout/stills/clip_XXX/clip_XXX_s01..s10.png.\n  See the blue note in the MODE A group for how to pick one.\n  (Mode A toggle = true now only previews the first frame, free.)\n\nSTEP 2 - MODE B (toggle = false) -> Blackout version of the clip\n  1. Pick the clip in node 1.\n  2. In node 2 set chosen_option to the still number you picked\n     (7 = clip_XXX_s07.png). Leave still_path_override empty and\n     stills_dir = blackout/stills.\n     (Override: paste e.g. blackout/stills/clip_001/clip_001_s07.png\n      into still_path_override. It wins over chosen_option, so clear\n      it before switching clips.)\n  3. Flip the toggle to B (false) and run.\n     B0 shows the still that was actually used - check it.\n     Node B1 picks the backend:\n       ltx23_quality_ref_v2v (default)  LTX 2.3 ref-v2v on fal, ~$0.27/clip\n       kling_o3_pro_edit   Kling O3 Edit Pro on fal, ~$0.85/clip\n       wan27_edit          Wan 2.7 on fal, ~$0.10/s\n     Only the backend you pick runs.\n  4. The result is conformed to the source's exact resolution, fps\n     and frame count, then saved:\n       output/blackout_ltx/targets/<clip>.mp4\n       output/blackout_ltx/pairs/<clip>_src.mp4\n     Read the pair report. Any padding/mismatch warning = check it.\n\nFALLBACK (bypassed, right of Mode A)\n  Old fal Nano Banana Pro stills (4+4+2, ~$1.50/clip). To use:\n  select those nodes, Ctrl+B, run Mode A. They save legacy\n  output/blackout/stills/<clip>_optNN.png, which Mode B still finds\n  if no Magnific still with that number exists.\n  fal spend guard: config.ini [spend_guard] ($2/session).\n\nSHORTCUTS\n  Ctrl+Enter run | Ctrl+M mute | Ctrl+B bypass | R refresh clips\n\n"
      ],
      "title": "READ ME - how this works",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
